index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7bf9382768110afade6a22c58e82878ec71bfc94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+## Context
+
+See `proposal.md` for motivation. `documents.py` builds two related catalog representations: `build_search_text` is embedded and persisted in Qdrant payloads by `indexer.py`; `build_lexical_text` is tokenized by `BM25Store`. Both presently contain raw name, headline fields, and selected/all properties. The matcher already sends an unchanged source tender query through hybrid retrieval and the existing reranker. The query-constraint module separately infers ball-valve type from product evidence, but its execution vocabulary is not available to retrieval documents.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- Generate a shared, pure set of retrieval descriptors from one product record.
+- Make execution and passage wording available to both retrieval modalities without deleting or devaluing catalog evidence.
+- Bound the descriptor vocabulary to explicit, inspectable signals and make classification tests table-driven.
+- Require a single controlled rebuild after implementation because the dense payload representation changes.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- No query rewriting, designation/alias mapping, LLM call, reranker prompt change, RRF tuning, or candidate selection rule.
+- No asserted equivalence between a legacy designation and an LD family.
+- No mutation of source CSV data, product fields, or public/hidden evaluation artifacts.
+- No inferred material, pressure, connection, temperature, product type, or special execution when source evidence is absent.
+
+## Decisions
+
+### Derive a bounded descriptor list from explicit evidence
+
+Add one pure catalog-document helper (or a small shared semantic helper if needed to avoid duplicated classification) that returns ordered Russian descriptor phrases. It inspects only the name plus established relevant properties such as `Тип продукта`, `Тип прохода`, and `Управление`. It recognizes an allowlist of explicit specialised expressions: underground installation, regulating/Regula, cryogenic, gas-specific, and electric-ready. It also maps explicit full and non-full/reduced passage evidence to the procurement phrases in the spec.
+
+This is preferable to an LLM document rewrite because deterministic source evidence is auditable and cannot hallucinate technical traits. It is preferable to a broad synonym dictionary because unsupported terms could silently alter candidate populations.
+
+### Treat ordinary execution as an exclusion-based, ball-valve-only descriptor
+
+For catalog records identified as ball valves, append `стандартное исполнение` only when the recognised-specialisation allowlist finds no positive signal. Keep specialised and passage descriptors independent: a regulating, non-full product carries both its specific execution and `стандартный проход`, but never the ordinary-execution descriptor.
+
+This distinguishes the two tender concepts while retaining raw text for unusual catalog terminology. The alternative of declaring every product without a marker `standard` is rejected because it could misrepresent non-ball-valve products; the alternative of omitting ordinary descriptors cannot test the observed ordinary-versus-specialised retrieval hypothesis.
+
+### Enrich both representations from the same descriptor source
+
+Append a labelled descriptor line to dense `search_text` and the corresponding terms to lexical text. Keep current source field order and property inclusion rules intact. `build_index` will naturally place the enriched dense text into future payloads, and a newly constructed `BM25Store` will use the enriched lexical corpus.
+
+This avoids a modality-only intervention and lets RRF receive a consistent representation. Reweighting RRF or changing result limits is rejected because it would confound index representation with fusion behavior.
+
+### Make rebuild and rollback explicit
+
+After focused unit tests pass, invoke the existing `scripts/build_index.py` workflow once against the standard catalog/collection configuration. Do not change the collection name or alias. Rollback is a code revert followed by rebuilding the same collection with the prior document representation; the source CSV remains untouched.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Catalog wording is ambiguous or has an unrecognised special execution] → Emit no specialised descriptor unless an allowlisted explicit phrase is present; preserve raw fields for retrieval.
+- [An ordinary descriptor raises a specialised product unexpectedly] → Never apply ordinary execution when an allowlisted special marker is present; test mutual exclusion.
+- [Dense and lexical representations drift] → Generate descriptors through one helper and test both document builders from the same fixtures.
+- [Rebuild changes operational data] → Use the existing rebuild script only after tests, record that exactly one rebuild is requested, and retain no CSV mutation path.
+- [Improved candidate recall still yields a poor final selection] → Preserve existing selection semantics so supervisor evaluation isolates this retrieval hypothesis; promotion remains guarded by blind safety metrics.
+
+## Migration Plan
+
+1. Implement the pure descriptor helper and append its output to both catalog document builders.
+2. Add unit tests for recognised explicit signals, ordinary/special mutual exclusion, passage terms, raw-text preservation, and BM25 visibility.
+3. Run the focused tests and `python -m pytest -q`.
+4. Run the existing index-build command once using the catalog CSV and configured Qdrant target.
+5. The outer supervisor conducts public/blind evaluation and promotion; those activities are not implementation tasks.
+6. If rejected, revert the representation change and rebuild the same collection from the untouched CSV.
