+++ b/openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+## Why
+
+The current retrieval documents preserve raw catalog text but lack a small, consistent representation of valve execution. As a result, ordinary tender requests can retrieve visually similar specialised variants, while catalog wording such as `Regula`, `для подземной установки`, or `под электропривод` is not expressed in the procurement vocabulary used by queries. This is now the highest-value untested retrieval mechanism: the hard-failure evidence includes specialised variants, whereas the previous selection filters and reranker-rubric experiments regressed safety or coverage.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add deterministic, catalog-derived execution descriptors to dense and BM25 document representations for ball valves.
+- Derive descriptors only from explicit product names and supported catalog properties; retain every original field and raw catalog term.
+- Represent ordinary versus explicitly specialised execution and explicit control-readiness concepts with stable, Russian procurement vocabulary.
+- Rebuild the catalog index after the document representation changes so existing indexed dense payloads use the enriched text.
+- Keep query canonicalization, candidate limits/fusion, reranker prompt, candidate filtering, and final-selection behavior unchanged.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `execution-aware-catalog-representation`: Produces bounded, deterministic execution descriptors in catalog retrieval documents while preserving raw catalog evidence.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected code: catalog document construction, BM25 corpus construction, dense-index construction, and focused document/BM25 tests.
+- Operational impact: one full catalog index rebuild is required after implementation; this consumes one of the harness's five permitted rebuilds.
+- No external API, model, prompt, or result-schema change is proposed.
